From 02a61d778d19aa18cdbf213ab440e29bbcaddc9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:15:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/47] NMXAccel: ordered VM-display flips - the flip waits for
 the surface's pixels, not WindowServer

WindowServer waited for the GPU to finish each frame
(commitAndWaitUntilSubmitted -> waitUntilCompleted in the plugin, twice per
frame: MetalContext::Flush and CoreDisplay's AccessComplete) so that the
blob flip found the copied-out pixels in place; its main thread spent ~35%
of a window drag blocked there and CPU and GPU work never overlapped.

The flip now runs on a thread call: a presented surface goes on the panel
once its IOSurface lock seed moved since it was last shown (the plugin's
copy-out of the new frame unlocks it for writing), capped at 100 ms; the
transaction completes through signalTransactionInterrupt. Sysctls
debug.nmxfb_blob_ordered (1; the plugin reads it), nmxfb_ord_waited,
nmxfb_ord_timeout, nmxfb_ord_wait_us. Three refusals in a row turn it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
